course: dictionary
lesson: 11337
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning the writer wants. Ask yourself what the sentence is about. In «Every country chooses its own money, called its currency: China the yuan (¥)», the sentence is about money, so yuan must be money.
explain: Capital letters are a clue too. «In 1337 China was ruled by the Mongol Yuan dynasty, which the Chinese Ming dynasty overthrew in 1368.» The capital Y and the word dynasty show that this Yuan is a family of rulers, not money. A dynasty is a line of rulers from one family.
explain: Check your choice by putting it back into the sentence. If the meaning makes sense, you have probably found the right one. If it does not, try another meaning, then check again.
fact: The yuan is the money of China.
fact: One yuan is divided into ten jiao or a hundred fen.
fact: The Yuan, with a capital Y, was a dynasty: a family of rulers that ruled China, started by the Mongol leader Kublai Khan.
fact: The official name of the money is renminbi.
fact: In Chinese, «yuán» also means round or first, but in English lessons about money or history, yuan means the money or the dynasty.
exercise: «China the yuan (¥)» is in a sentence about money. What is the yuan? | *The money of China | A family of rulers | A kind of tea | A round shape
exercise: «In 1337 China was ruled by the Mongol Yuan dynasty.» What does Yuan mean here? | A Chinese meal | *A family of rulers that ruled China | A family of rulers | Money used in shops
exercise: In «Every country chooses its own money, called its currency», which symbol is written next to yuan? | ₴ | £ | *¥ | €
test: «Ukraine has the hryvnia, China the yuan, Japan the yen.» Which country uses the yuan? | *China | Japan | Nigeria | Ukraine
test: Renminbi is the official name of what? | A family of rulers | The Mongol leader Kublai Khan | A round shape | *The money of China
exam: «The Yuan ended when floods, famine and rebellions shook it, and Zhu Yuanzhang took Beijing in 1368.» In this sentence, what is the Yuan? | *A family of rulers that ruled China | Money used in shops | A river in Beijing | A round coin
